MongoDB Basics 2
Practical 2 in your journal uses a collection of user documents and performs insert, update, add field, delete, count, and projection operations.     BDNS Journal
We will use the same 2-CMD college setup.
Step 1 — Start MongoDB Server
CMD 1
mongod

Keep this window open.
CMD 2
mongo

You should get:
>

Step 2 — Select/Create the database
use Data

Output:
switched to db Data

Step 3 — Insert the documents
The journal uses documents with these fields:
- Name
- Age
- Country
- Gender
Enter:
db.col.insertMany([
  {Name:"Romal",Age:20,Country:"India",Gender:"Female"},
  {Name:"Raj",Age:12,Country:"Russia",Gender:"Male"},
  {Name:"Rajiv",Age:25,Country:"USA",Gender:"Male"},
  {Name:"Suja",Age:65,Country:"India",Gender:"Female"},
  {Name:"Koyal",Age:30,Country:"USA",Gender:"Female"}
])

Output
{
  "acknowledged" : true,
  "insertedIds" : {
    "0" : ObjectId("..."),
    "1" : ObjectId("..."),
    "2" : ObjectId("..."),
    "3" : ObjectId("..."),
    "4" : ObjectId("...")
  }
}

Your ObjectId values will be different.

Step 4 — Display all documents
db.col.find()

Output
You should see the five inserted documents:
